From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: sheng: select UTMI as the USB2-only PIPE clock

Sheng's boot DT deliberately enables only the eUSB2 PHY. U-Boot's
dwc3_qcom_glue_configure() in v2026.10-rc5 selects the UTMI clock in place
of the unavailable SuperSpeed PIPE clock only when this property exists.
Match that contract rather than relying on ABL's controller state.

This changes only the U-Boot DT; Linux retains its full USB3/DP setup.
---
diff --git a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/qcom/sm8550-xiaomi-sheng.dts b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/qcom/sm8550-xiaomi-sheng.dts
--- a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/qcom/sm8550-xiaomi-sheng.dts
+++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/qcom/sm8550-xiaomi-sheng.dts
@@ -128,6 +128,7 @@
 	phys = <&usb_1_hsphy>;
 	phy-names = "usb2-phy";
 	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk;
 	maximum-speed = "high-speed";
 	status = "okay";
 };
